    {
      "title": "2. APA 7th edition — author-date system",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Parenthetical: \"Working memory degrades under cognitive load (Smith, 2024).\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#2-apa-7th-edition-author-date-system",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Narrative: \"Smith (2024) found that working memory degrades under cognitive load.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#2-apa-7th-edition-author-date-system",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Direct quotes require a page or paragraph number: \"(Smith, 2024, p. 42)\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#2-apa-7th-edition-author-date-system",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Signal phrases — integrating sources into prose",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Signal-phrase verbs carry stance:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#3-signal-phrases-integrating-sources-into-prose",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Neutral: notes, states, reports, observes, describes, writes",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#3-signal-phrases-integrating-sources-into-prose",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Argumentative: argues, contends, claims, asserts, maintains",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#3-signal-phrases-integrating-sources-into-prose",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Evidence-based: found, demonstrated, showed, established, documented",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#3-signal-phrases-integrating-sources-into-prose",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Hedged: suggests, proposes, hypothesizes, speculates, implies",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#3-signal-phrases-integrating-sources-into-prose",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Critical: disputes, challenges, questions, complicates, refutes",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#3-signal-phrases-integrating-sources-into-prose",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Pseudo-citation — the failure mode",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "\"Studies show...\" with no citation is pseudo-citation. Three repairs:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#4-pseudo-citation-the-failure-mode",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Name the source. \"Studies show\" → \"Cowan (2010) and Baddeley (2012) showed\".",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#4-pseudo-citation-the-failure-mode",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Drop the unsupportable claim. If you cannot find a citation, you do not yet have evidence.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#4-pseudo-citation-the-failure-mode",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Mark it as your own argument. \"I argue that...\" is honest.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#4-pseudo-citation-the-failure-mode",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Primary, secondary, tertiary sources",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Primary - original research, raw data, firsthand accounts.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#5-primary-secondary-tertiary-sources",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Secondary - analysis or interpretation of primary sources.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#5-primary-secondary-tertiary-sources",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Tertiary - compilations of secondary sources. Wikipedia, encyclopedias.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#5-primary-secondary-tertiary-sources",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Persistent identifiers",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "DOI (Digital Object Identifier) - Format 10.xxxx/yyyy. Include as https://doi.org/10.xxxx/yyyy. Required by APA 7, IEEE.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#6-persistent-identifiers",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "ORCID - persistent identifier for an author.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#6-persistent-identifiers",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "arXiv ID - preprints in physics, CS, math.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#6-persistent-identifiers",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Toulmin argument structure",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Claim - the conclusion you want the reader to accept.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#7-toulmin-argument-structure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Grounds (data, evidence) - the facts that support the claim.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#7-toulmin-argument-structure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Warrant - the underlying principle that lets the grounds support the claim.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#7-toulmin-argument-structure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Backing - support for the warrant itself.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#7-toulmin-argument-structure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Qualifier - limits on the claim.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#7-toulmin-argument-structure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Rebuttal - counterclaims and exceptions acknowledged.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/academic-and-citation-writing/#7-toulmin-argument-structure",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
